# derived-fence-binding: seed.sh copies the read set of the arms it selects (I75 I108 I121 I122 I123) into the
# pristine tree the batteries mutate and run the enforcement-map validator in: the prologue's inputs, the
# --arms map renderer, core/team-roles/, core/scripts/*.sh and this fixture's own directory. templates/,
# patterns/ and .claude/rules/ are not copied: plant_root creates the root it plants in. .githooks/ is
# undeclared and unstaged: no selected arm opens it.
!scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
scripts/render-invariant-index.sh
core/skills/ai-dlc/steps/gate-validation.md
core/skills/ai-dlc/enforcement-map.yaml
core/skills/ai-dlc/core-manifest.md
core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/setup-sites.md
core/skills/ai-dlc-update/fixture-manifest.md
# reason: I108/I121/I122/I123 take core/team-roles/*.md as their population, and its listing is an input.
core/team-roles/
# reason: I75's subject set is core/scripts/*.sh by glob (validate-enforcement-map.sh:6160), so the listing is an input.
core/scripts/
core/fixtures/lib/mutant.sh
core/fixtures/lib/report.sh
core/fixtures/lib/layout.sh
